A **QoS flow** is identified by a QoS Flow Identifier (QFI) and is associated with a set of QoS parameters (e.g. 5QI, guaranteed‑/maximum‑bit‑rate, averaging window, etc.) that are signalled to the UE together with the QoS rule(s) that refer to that flow【5†L1-L4】.  

A **signalled QoS rule** that the network sends to the UE contains the following elements【1†L4-L9】:

* an indication of whether the rule is the default QoS rule (DQR);  
* a QoS‑rule identifier (QRI) that is unique within the PDU session;  
* the QFI of the associated QoS flow;  
* optionally a set of packet filters (UL, DL or both); and  
* a precedence value.  

If the rule is the default QoS rule for an IP‑type or Ethernet‑type PDU session, the packet‑filter set must not be empty and, when a match‑all filter is present, the highest precedence value shall be used【1†L10-L15】.  

Thus, a QoS flow is defined by its QFI and associated QoS parameters, and a signalled QoS rule includes the default‑rule flag, QRI, QFI, optional packet‑filter set, and precedence value.
